1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,950
Have you ever seen white steam coming up from the streets of New York?

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:07,700
Under Manhattan, there are pipes full of hot steam.

3
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:12,450
They started in 1882. Now they are over 160 km long.

4
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:15,900
Power plants make the steam and send it to 1,500 buildings.

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:19,600
The steam heats buildings, and in summer it even runs air conditioners.

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,350
Hospitals also use it to clean surgery tools.

7
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:28,100
Most street steam comes from rain hitting the hot pipes.

8
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:31,850
New York is really a city with a giant boiler underground.
